Everything is in place: my slot lease is released (slot 1 now held by a peer), and my only source edits are `impl/gen_batchlane.c` and `strategies/gen_batchlane.md`.

**Summary of the round:** gen_pfa_small's r4 record called out my L=15 register-explicit pencil as the loser it was. Same-core racing on a held lease confirmed it, but with a twist: the pencil *form* was only ~0.2% of the gap — the real cost was the map tail. On the memory-form pencil, one exact `vdivpd` beats my rcp14+2NR ladder by 4%, while at 10/12 (register pencils) the ladder still wins. I shipped L=15 as the r2-lineage memory form (fused DFT5X2 pair for the equal-slot-set groups) + vdivpd tail, keeping 10/12/20 untouched (bit-identical outputs to r4 there). A new hybrid form (register sweeps + memory map x-pass) was built, raced, and rejected at +0.35%. All gates pass at all four sizes including B=1/B=9/B=12 remainder paths, and the L=15 board gap to gen_pfa_small (4.566 vs 4.429) should now close to parity or better.

Technique ended on: memory-form PFA pencils + fused vdivpd map at L=15 (register+rcp kept at 10/12, memory+div at 20); best node numbers — batched: 1.157 / 1.915 / **4.410** / 13.04 us at L=10/12/15/20, B=1: 10.65 / 17.59 / 40.53 / 133.97 us; rel L2 single call 2.6–3.1e-16, two-step 8.2e-16–1.2e-15, graded chains 4.4e-14–1.7e-13 (all tolerances met with ≥25x margin).
